## 9. FIX EDITING, PUBLISHING AND DUPLICATION

Tutors must be able to return to an existing examination, make edits, save it and republish it where allowed.

Saving an existing examination must update the same record rather than create a duplicate.

Preserve the examination ID and assignment relationships through editing.

Published examinations with existing attempts must be versioned or snapshotted appropriately. Editing future exam settings must not silently change the meaning or grading of historical attempts.

Respect completed/closed states and existing lifecycle safeguards.

If a tutor wants to reuse an examination as the foundation for another examination, provide an explicit **Duplicate Examination** action with a clear new ID and deliberate treatment of settings. Do not interpret an ordinary Save or Publish action as duplication.

Tutor ownership and school-assignment permissions must be checked server-side for read, create, update, publish, republish, delete and import operations.

## 10. KEEP SCHOOL AND TUTOR PERMISSIONS STRICT

Tutors must see only the schools and examinations they are authorised to manage. Their school selectors, question-bank importers, reports and access-code views must all respect the same permissions.

School administrators must be able to view their own school's assigned upcoming examinations, history and permitted access codes, but must not be able to create examinations, edit questions, publish exams or alter grading configurations.

School administrators must not see other schools in school lists or obtain other schools' records by manipulating a URL, query parameter or request body.

Enforce these boundaries in server-side functions and Firestore rules, not only by hiding UI controls.

Platform administrators must retain legitimate cross-school capabilities.

Do not expose answer keys, protected question-bank details, unreleased marks or private tutor feedback through school access-code or reporting endpoints.

## 11. STUDENT EXAMINATION EXPERIENCE

Students must be able to distinguish examinations built on Jaystarbliss from external-link examinations.

For a native examination, display the appropriate title, schedule, instructions and available start action. Enforce passcodes, eligibility, opening/closing times and attempt limits. After submission, show the result only according to the examination's release settings.

For an external-link examination, display the exam information and a clear **Open Examination** action. Validate the student's portal access and assignment before granting access to the external URL.

When an examination is assigned to a student's class, ensure it appears in the student's appropriate upcoming-exams view and relevant dashboard notification. Notifications must not duplicate each time the student refreshes the page.

Preserve the current result and examination-history experience.

## 12. RESULT INTEGRITY AND REPORT CONSISTENCY

Use a consistent authoritative scoring model.

For example:

- One mark out of three must display as 1/3 and approximately 33.33%.
- Four marks out of ten must display as 4/10 and 40%.
- An examination explicitly worth 100 marks may display out of 100.

Never default an unknown denominator to 100 without evidence.

For legacy attempts with missing total marks, derive the denominator from the applicable persisted question definition or attempt snapshot where possible. If it cannot be reconstructed safely, handle it explicitly.

Ensure that the same marks, percentage and grade are displayed in student, tutor, parent and school views where each role is authorised to see the result.

Use the same released-result report renderer for student-facing results and individual staff PDF downloads. Keep the correct partner school's name in reports; do not use Jaystarbliss as a generic substitute for the actual assigned partner school.

Preserve historical attempt snapshots when examination questions or marks are edited.

If the current system supports bulk PDF exports, ensure they reuse the same template and authorised result data. If the school administrator has a bulk-report workflow that needs completion, add or repair a dedicated action to download individual reports as PDFs in a ZIP while preserving existing Excel exports.

